# Crockpot API — GET /me
#
# Own file, own login: REST Client's captured variables and cookie jar
# are scoped per .http file, not shared across files, so this can't
# chain off requests/auth.http's login — it does its own, right at the
# top, using the same confirmed password account auth.http sets up (run
# its ✅ register + ✅ confirm sections once first if you haven't on
# this dev DB). Fill in your real email/password below.
#
# Also the real end-to-end proof that AuthMiddleware (CROC-003) works
# against a live request — no prior ticket exercised it outside its own
# unit tests. See requests/README.md for setup/running instructions.


# ══════════════════════════════════════════
#  GET /me
# ══════════════════════════════════════════

### Login, to get a token for the checks below.
# @name login
POST http://localhost:{{$dotenv PORT}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "REPLACE_WITH_YOUR_REAL_EMAIL",
  "password": "correcthorsebattery"
}

###

@authToken = {{login.response.body.accessToken}}

### ✅ 200 — returns the authenticated user's profile
GET http://localhost:{{$dotenv PORT}}/me
Authorization: Bearer {{authToken}}

###

### 🔒 401 — no token
GET http://localhost:{{$dotenv PORT}}/me

###

### 🔒 401 — malformed token
GET http://localhost:{{$dotenv PORT}}/me
Authorization: Bearer not-a-valid-token


# ══════════════════════════════════════════
#  Cleanup
# ══════════════════════════════════════════

### Re-run the Login request above once more first, so @authToken is
### freshly issued (well inside its 15-minute expiry) going into the
### check below — otherwise a 401 there could just mean the token
### expired, not that the user is gone.

### Deletes the same shared test account requests/auth.http uses — only
### run this once you're done testing against it for this session; run
### auth.http's own ✅ register + ✅ confirm sections again afterward
### before its account-dependent sections will work. Connect via
### psql/a DB client:
#
#   DELETE FROM users WHERE email = 'REPLACE_WITH_YOUR_REAL_EMAIL';
#

### 🔒 401 — GET /me with the now-stale @authToken from the freshly
### re-issued login above, run immediately after the DELETE. Proves the
### valid-token-but-deleted-user path (CROC-009's RefreshToken/Me fix)
### for real, not just against a mock.
GET http://localhost:{{$dotenv PORT}}/me
Authorization: Bearer {{authToken}}
